  "note": "Triennial election of the rural district council (29 divisions), 1964: sixteen contests at the close of nominations, fifteen after the withdrawal of Bernard Murphy in Belleek, polled 4 June 1964. Polled 4 June 1964, counted 5 June. A vacant seat after the death of Thomas Cassidy. McKevitt lost his deposit. The printed poll (536) is ten more than the votes and spoilt papers (526). Hollywood is \"Thomas K. Hollywood\" and Clarke \"Daniel Clarke, Lower Killeen\" in the nominations."
